# XCU crontab
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The tests replace the invoking user's crontab entry, so each of them first
# saves the existing one with crontab -l and puts it back (or removes it with
# crontab -r when there was none) on every exit path. The entries used run the
# command true on 30 February, a day that does not exist, so no job can run.
# A user who is not allowed to use crontab (the XSI access files) makes the
# first installation fail; the tests then report UNRESOLVED. The default
# environment of a job, the run of a job and mail are not exercised. -e is
# shaded UP.

assertion  XCU.crontab.001
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#STDOUT
class      required
says       crontab FILE installs the entries of FILE and crontab -l then writes
           them to standard output with exit status zero (comment and blank
           lines may differ).
test       t/001-install-and-list.sh

assertion  XCU.crontab.002
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#STDIN
class      required
says       Without a file operand crontab reads the entries from standard input
           and installs them.
test       t/002-install-from-stdin.sh

assertion  XCU.crontab.003
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       Installing a second entry file replaces the first: after it, the
           listing holds the lines of the second file and none of the first.
test       t/003-replace.sh

assertion  XCU.crontab.004
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#OPTIONS
class      required
says       crontab -r removes the entry with exit status zero, after which the
           listing holds none of the removed entries.
test       t/004-remove.sh

assertion  XCU.crontab.005
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#CONSEQUENCES OF ERRORS
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
says       crontab of a file that does not exist exits with a status above
           zero and leaves the installed entry as it was.
test       t/005-missing-file.sh

assertion  XCU.crontab.006
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
class      conditional
when       UP
says       crontab -e runs the editor named by EDITOR on a copy of the entry
           and installs the result: an editor that appends a line gives an
           entry that holds the old lines and the new one.
test       t/006-edit.sh

assertion  XCU.crontab.007
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/crontab.html#INPUT FILES
class      untestable
says       A job runs with HOME, LOGNAME, PATH and SHELL set (SHELL naming sh)
           whatever the values when crontab was run; the fields of a line
           select minutes, hours, days, months and weekdays as stated, a percent
           sign in the command becomes a newline, and the remaining lines are
           standard input of the command.
reason     A job runs only when its time comes, under the scheduler daemon;
           a test cannot wait for it within a bounded time.
